# Cross-Evaluation System: CHALO Ground Truth vs Engine Outputs

## Problem Statement

Before running `transit_kashmir_v3.py` in production, we need a calibration loop that compares the engine's predictions against **real-world CHALO data** to tune parameters until the model matches observed reality. The three Chalo datasets provide ground truth at three different granularities:

| Dataset | Granularity | Key Metrics |
|---|---|---|
| **Ridership Data.csv** | Monthly, system-wide | Total ridership, EPKM, trip count, operated KM, scheduled KM |
| **Route Wise deployed Buses.csv** | Per-route, static | Fleet deployed per SSCL route (9m vs 12m split) |
| **Hourly Passenger Count.csv** | Hourly, system-wide | Hour-by-hour demand shape (April 2026) |

