## What Can Actually Be Compared

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The CHALO data and the engine output operate at **different granularities**. Not everything maps 1:1. Here's what's feasible:

### Level 1: System-Wide Aggregates (Ridership Data.csv ↔ Engine Totals)

| CHALO Metric | Engine Equivalent | How to Compare |
|---|---|---|
| **Total ridership/month** (~9.5–12L pax) | `Population_Served × mode_share × trip_rate × days/month` | Derive implied daily pax from pop served + assumptions |
| **Operated KM/month** (~5.0–5.9L km) | `Σ(Route_KM × 2 × trips_per_day × days)` where `trips_per_day = service_hours / Headway_Min` | Direct calculation from fleet plan |
| **Scheduled KM/month** (~6.5–6.7L km) | Same but using 100% schedule (no cancellations) | Direct calculation |
| **Trip Count/month** (~25K–28K) | `Σ(service_hours / Headway_Min) × days_per_month` for all active routes | Direct calculation |
| **EPKM** (₹10–14 cash) | Requires fare assumption — sanity check only | Informational |
| **Op Ratio** (Operated/Scheduled ~82–90%) | Engine already has `CHALO_OP_RATIO = 0.845` | Verify engine assumption matches latest data |

### Level 2: Route-Level Fleet Match (Route Wise deployed Buses.csv ↔ Engine Fleet)

| CHALO Metric | Engine Equivalent | How to Compare |
|---|---|---|
| **Buses deployed per route** (1–7) | `Fleet_Required` from Step 8 | Direct 1:1 comparison for 30 SSCL routes |
| **9m vs 12m split** | `MPV_Count` vs `HPV_Count` | Compare vehicle type distribution |
| **Total fleet** (98 buses) | `Σ Fleet_Required` (SSCL routes only) | Aggregate match |

### Level 3: Temporal Demand Shape (Hourly Passenger Count.csv ↔ Headway Design)

| CHALO Metric | Engine Equivalent | How to Compare |
|---|---|---|
| **Peak hour** (9 AM, ~4300–5000 pax) | `CHALO_PEAK_PAX_PER_HOUR = 4346` | Verify constant calibration |
| **Peak-to-trough ratio** (~10:1) | Engine uses flat headway (no time-of-day variation) | Diagnose headway waste in off-peak |
| **Weekday vs weekend shape** | Not in engine (no day-type differentiation) | Flag for v4 |
| **Service window** (6 AM – 10 PM) | `CHALO_SERVICE_START_HR = 6`, `CHALO_SERVICE_END_HR = 22` | Verify |

