#### Calibration Parameters & Their Sensitivities:

The script will output a **parameter sensitivity table** showing which engine constants to adjust:

| If Engine Output Is... | Likely Cause | Parameter to Tune |
|---|---|---|
| Fleet too high vs CHALO | Headway too aggressive or cycle time too conservative | `HEADWAY_HP_MIN`, `CONGESTION_CITY_CORE`, `STOP_PENALTY_MIN` |
| Fleet too low vs CHALO | Headway too relaxed or cycle time underestimated | Same parameters, opposite direction |
| Operated KM too high | Too many routes active, or routes too long | `OVERLAP_THRESHOLD`, `TRUNK_CDI_GATE_PERCENTILE` |
| Ridership overestimated | Population walkshed too generous | `WALK_CATCHMENT_M`, `VIRTUAL_STOP_SPACING_M` |
| Wrong vehicle mix | HPV/MPV split formula off | Step 9 split ratios (0.85/0.15) |

#### Output Files:
- `calibration_report_v3.md` — Markdown report with comparison tables
- `calibration_charts/` — PNG charts (fleet scatter, KM histogram, hourly demand overlay)
- Console summary with pass/fail indicators

