## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Mode share assumption** — To convert `Population_Served` to implied ridership, we need a transit mode share. The Census 2011 modal split for Srinagar UA is ~5–8% public transport. Should we use 6% as baseline, or do you have a more recent estimate from SSCL/SMA?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Trip rate** — Average daily trips per person using transit. Typical Indian Tier-2 cities use 1.2–1.5. The CHALO data implies ~40,000 daily pax across 98 buses. Should we back-calculate from this?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q3: Scope of "good match"** — What tolerance do you consider acceptable? For fleet-level comparisons, ±20% per route is typical for planning models. For system KM totals, ±15% is standard. Want tighter thresholds?

